1
00:00:03,051 --> 00:00:05,523
Tonight, the Moon is a thin crescent.

2
00:00:05,573 --> 00:00:07,908
Last week, it was completely round!

3
00:00:07,958 --> 00:00:10,003
Did someone eat a piece of it?

4
00:00:10,845 --> 00:00:12,817
Mila drew it all: every night,

5
00:00:12,867 --> 00:00:14,569
the Moon changes a little.

6
00:00:14,619 --> 00:00:16,978
And yet, it's always the same Moon!

7
00:00:17,762 --> 00:00:19,276
Discovery mission!

8
00:00:21,792 --> 00:00:22,474
Mini mode!

9
00:00:22,524 --> 00:00:24,232
The Sun always lights up

10
00:00:24,282 --> 00:00:25,771
one half of the Moon.

11
00:00:25,821 --> 00:00:26,284
Always!

12
00:00:26,334 --> 00:00:28,751
The other half stays in the dark.

13
00:00:29,541 --> 00:00:30,897
But the Moon goes around

14
00:00:30,947 --> 00:00:32,127
the Earth in a month.

15
00:00:32,177 --> 00:00:33,006
From your home,

16
00:00:33,056 --> 00:00:36,571
you see its lit half from an angle that changes every night.

17
00:00:38,540 --> 00:00:40,600
A small piece: a crescent.

18
00:00:40,650 --> 00:00:42,385
Half of it: a quarter.

19
00:00:42,435 --> 00:00:45,144
The whole lit half: the full Moon!

20
00:00:45,194 --> 00:00:46,442
Then it shrinks…

21
00:00:46,492 --> 00:00:48,115
and it starts again.

22
00:00:48,880 --> 00:00:51,971
Seen from space, Curio sees the Moon half and half:

23
00:00:52,021 --> 00:00:54,928
one side facing the Sun, the other in the night.

24
00:00:54,978 --> 00:00:56,333
It never lost a piece!

25
00:00:57,128 --> 00:00:59,348
That's why the Moon changes shape.

26
00:01:00,669 --> 00:01:02,967
The Moon is always half lit by the Sun;

27
00:01:03,017 --> 00:01:05,185
it's our viewing angle that changes.

28
00:01:06,169 --> 00:01:08,708
With an adult, in the dark: a lamp,

29
00:01:08,758 --> 00:01:10,706
and a ball at arm's length.

30
00:01:10,756 --> 00:01:14,381
Turn around slowly: crescent, quarter, full Moon!

31
00:01:15,160 --> 00:01:17,812
And why do we hear thunder after lightning?

32
00:01:17,862 --> 00:01:19,119
The answer tomorrow.
